// NEGATIVE TEST -- a macro body may not contain a float literal (N3-12).
//
// The float half of the literal-kind loss that tests/reject/macro_body_string_literal.pd
// pins for strings, and it is pinned separately because the SILENT OUTCOME was
// different and both were measured. `AstToken::Literal` is a `String` carrying
// no kind, and the reverse conversion guesses with `parse::<i64>()`, which fails
// for `3.5` -- so the literal came back as a `Token::String`.
//
// Measured at e8eb1a9, compiling and running with no diagnostic:
//     macro pi!() { 3.5 }
//     fn main() { print(pi!()); }
// printed `3.5` -- the four characters, as a String. Used as the number it
// looks like, the same macro failed with "Type mismatch: expected Float, found
// String", which is the same defect wearing a diagnostic.
macro pi!() { 3.5 }

fn main() {
    print_int(1);
}
